; fib — the classic fork-join demonstration and the worst case for it: two
; recursive calls and no work of their own per node. `fib(n - 1) + fib(n - 2)`
; is the plain pattern; the engine runs the two calls in parallel near the top
; of the recursion and leaves the deep levels to a plain copy of the
; function.

function fib(n: int) returns int
{
    if n < 2
        return n
    fib(n - 1) + fib(n - 2)
}

print("fib 42: `fib(42)`")
